{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.WronskianIndex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.WronskianIndex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.MvGenWronskian","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothIndex","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_max_le_index_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_max_le_index_det","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L254-L299","doc":"**The bridge.**  A lower bound `θ` on `index P`, plus a per-column cost bound\n`t + j/rr` on the operator lists `D i j`, gives the truncated-sum lower bound on the\ndeterminant's index.\n\nThe `max 0` is the whole point: `index_le_index_pderivList_add` gives\n`index P ≤ index (∂_{D i j} P) + cost`, so column `j` contributes at least `θ − t − j/rr`\n*only while that is positive*; past the cut-off all it contributes is `index ≥ 0`.  A\nformulation without the `max` would be false for every column past `(θ−t)·rr`.\n\nNote the permutation `p₀`: `index_det_ge` bounds `index (det M)` below by the `Finset.inf`\nover permutations, so we pick the minimising one and bound *its* diagonal.  The cost\nhypothesis is uniform in `i`, so the choice of `p₀` costs nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coe_sub_le_of_le_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coe_sub_le_of_le_add","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L240-L252","doc":"Subtraction against a `WithTop ℚ` upper summand.\n\n`WithTop ℚ` has no subtraction worth using, so `θ ≤ x + c ⊢ θ − c ≤ x` has to be done by\ncase-splitting on `x = ⊤` and descending to `ℚ` on the other branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coe_sum_withTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coe_sum_withTop","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L229-L238","doc":"Casting a rational sum into `WithTop ℚ` distributes over the sum.\n\n`WithTop ℚ` has no `RingHom` from `ℚ` to push through (it is not a semiring), so this is\nproved by induction on the `Finset` rather than by `map_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_index_mvGenWronskian_bound_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_index_mvGenWronskian_bound_tight","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L196-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_index_le_index_det_pderivList_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_index_le_index_det_pderivList_add","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L147-L183","doc":"**The index of a determinant of operators applied to a single polynomial.**\n\n`sum_index_le_index_mvGenWronskian_add` covers a *family* `f`, with one operator list per row.\nThe separated factorisation of `QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedWronskian.lean` produces something else:\na matrix whose `(i,j)` entry is a *mixed* operator `Dx i ++ Dy j` applied to **one**\npolynomial `P`.  Nothing covered that, and it is what turns \"`P` has large index\" into \"its\nWronskian has large index\".\n\nSame proof shape as the family version — evaluate `index_det_ge`'s infimum at a permutation\nattaining it, then bound each entry by `index_le_index_pderivList_add`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_map_inv_le_length_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_map_inv_le_length_div","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L127-L145","doc":"**The differentiation cost of a list is at most its length over the smallest degree.**\n\n`∑_{k ∈ l} 1/dₖ ≤ |l| / D` when `D ≤ dₖ` for every `k`.  This is what turns the abstract cost\nhypothesis of the bounds below into something concrete. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_index_le_index_mvGenWronskian_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_index_le_index_mvGenWronskian_add","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L86-L125","doc":"**The index of a generalized Wronskian:**\n\n    ∑ᵢ index (f i)  ≤  index (mvGenWronskian D f)  +  m · C\n\nwhen every operator list has differentiation cost at most `C`.\n\nThe composite `index_det_ge` alone does not give: that bounds the determinant by the indices\nof its *entries*, which are `pderivList (D i) (f j)`, and it is\n`index_le_index_pderivList_add` that carries those back to the `f`.\n\nThe proof evaluates the infimum in `index_det_ge` at a permutation attaining it — `Perm (Fin m)`\nis a non-empty fintype, so one exists — and then bounds that permutation's sum termwise.  It\nis the same shape as `abs_coeff_mvGenWronskian_le`, run in the opposite order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_le_index_pderivList_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_le_index_pderivList_add","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L59-L84","doc":"**Iterated differentiation costs at most `∑_{j ∈ l} 1/dⱼ` of index.**\n\nThe list form of `index_le_index_pderiv_add`.  Each step of `pderivList` can drop the index by\nat most `1/dⱼ` for the variable `j` differentiated, and the costs add. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.nsmul_coe_withTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.nsmul_coe_withTop","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/WronskianIndex.lean#L47-L57","doc":"`WithTop ℚ` is not a semiring, so `nsmul_eq_mul` does not apply to it; this is the\nreplacement the `Finset.sum_const` step needs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}